      "provenance": "literature_retrieved",
      "rationale": "Six independent ledger lines (L1\u2013L6) all explicitly name the junction between residues 371 and 372 in full-length human CaSR as the insertion site for FLAG or Myc epitopes. Python verification confirms residue 371 = D and residue 372 = T, both within the extracellular span 20\u2013612, 242 residues from the nearest TM boundary (613). The authors describe this as a 'functionally silent loop in the ECD', and the tagged constructs are used routinely for surface ELISA, co-IP, and TRF assays across multiple publications. Full-length human CaSR with FLAG (DYKDDDDK) or Myc (EQKLISEEDL) epitope inserted between residues 371 and 372 in the VFT domain ECD loop, transiently transfected in HEK-293 cells; described as a 'functionally silent loop in the ECD'.",
      "residue_after": "T",
      "residue_before": "D",
      "residue_label": "D371",
      "residue_range": null,
      "site_id": "CASR-internal-371-lit",
